erates $174K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $54K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Sphere Entertainment Co. is a mid-cap communication services business with a $4.3B market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -11% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are contracting by -3.7pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at -4% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $191M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 16 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 7.28\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -3.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.2%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 6.7% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -3.7pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Price sits 8032% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":80.32423462607915},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (36.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Communication Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 28% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 59/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Communication Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Financial quality scores above most Communication Services peers"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Sphere Entertainment (SPHR) Reported $274.26 Million In Q3 Revenue","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/sphere-entertainment-sphr-reported-274-211737109.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793999857.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.963,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Sphere Entertainment (SPHR) Could Be 30% Undervalued On Q3 Revenue Beat And New Content","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/media/nyse-sphr/sphere-entertainment/news/sphere-entertainment-sphr-could-be-30-undervalued-on-q3-reve","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793