ings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.2% (1.2% in buybacks).","The share count has grown 8.5% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","Short interest is elevated at 36.5% of the float, 8.0 days to cover."],"people":["With about 1,100 employees, each generates about $1.1M of revenue, 1.8x the Communication Services median, and productivity has risen 9.8% a year.","That works out to $174K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.3M (1x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (10/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $54K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":26,"head":"Avoid: priced 8032% above its fair value of $1.48.","pros":["FCF margin 15.7%","Revenue grew 9.8%/yr over 5y","Piotroski F-score 7/9","13 analysts' mean target $157 (+30%)","12-1 month momentum +44%"],"cons":["Model rating PASS (composite 8, gates 4/23)","Trades 8032% above fair value of $1.48","ROIC 3.8% vs WACC 9.7%","Net debt/EBITDA 7.8x","Interest coverage only -3.8x"],"flags":["Priced 8032% above its fair value of $1.48","Altman Z in the distress zone (1.38)","Operating income covers interest only -3.8x","The model rates it PASS"],"need":[],"buy_below":1.25,"vc":{"base":1.48,"base_src":"dcf","bear":0.0,"bull":9.97,"alt_median":20.05,"n_alt":1,"gap":-0.9264,"dispersion":0.8629,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","models disagree (86% dispersion)","DCF is 93% below the other models' median ($20.05)","the bear case is a wipeout"]},"med":{"pe":14.9123,"ev_ebitda":9.366,"pfcf":11.3182,"pb":1.9143,"roic":0.0635,"gross_margin":0.5527,"fcf_margin":0.1346,"div_yield":0.0323}},"ticker":"SPHR","date":"2026-11-06"}